# Everything the image does not need. Keeping the build context small keeps
# builds fast and stops local state leaking into an image.
#
# Note what is NOT excluded: `ml/` is required, because the image trains the
# model during the build. Only the *generated artifact* is excluded, so the
# build always trains its own rather than copying whatever a developer happens
# to have lying around.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

tests/
pytest.ini

ml/artifacts/
*.joblib
*.pkl

.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
